  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "How, how much, how often",
      "title_cz": "Jak, jak moc, jak často",
      "diagram": "scale",
      "labels": [
        "hardly",
        "slightly",
        "fairly",
        "completely"
      ],
      "body": "66 adverbs. An adverb never names a thing — it says something about the action, or about another word: how it happens, how much, how often, or how sure you are.\nMost of them are an adjective plus -ly: quick → quickly, easy → easily, careful → carefully.",
      "body_cz": "Příslovce neoznačuje věc — říká, jak, jak moc, jak často nebo jak jistě se něco děje. Většina vzniká z přídavného jména příponou -ly."
    },
    {
      "title": "What each one tells you",
      "title_cz": "Co které říká",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Tells you",
          "Words in this unit"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "how · jak",
            "quickly, slowly, quietly, carefully, badly"
          ],
          [
            "how much · jak moc",
            "completely, extremely, slightly, almost"
          ],
          [
            "how often · jak často",
            "usually, normally, rarely, constantly"
          ],
          [
            "how sure · jak jistě",
            "probably, certainly, obviously, perhaps"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "note": "hardly is not the adverb of hard. hard = tvrdě, usilovně; hardly = stěží, skoro ne. I work hard and I hardly work are opposites.",
      "note_cz": "Pozor: hardly ≠ hard. hardly = stěží / skoro ne."
    }
  ],
